-- title:
--   Hecke multiset families for Eichler orders and Fuchsian descent
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q,q'$ be primes such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: $a>0$ or $b>0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $N\neq 0$, let $\Lambda,R$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules with $\Lambda$ a maximal order, $R$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$) and $R\le\Lambda$, and let $\iota:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map. Then there is a family $H$ assigning to each prime $\ell$ a multiset of elements of $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ such that, for each prime $\ell$, there is a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with: every $x\in S$ lies in $R$, has $\mathrm{nrd}\,x=\ell$, and satisfies $x\otimes 1=h$ for some $h$ in the idelic Hecke set $\mathcal{S}_\ell$ — namely `levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ` (those $h\in$ `primeHeckeSet R ℓ` with $h R h^{-1}\neq R$ and $R\not\le h\Lambda h^{-1}$, in the finite-adelic sense) if $\ell\mid N$, and `primeHeckeSet R ℓ` (units $h$ of the finite-adelic algebra with $h$ and $\ell h^{-1}$ in the adelic box of $R$, but $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}h$ not in it) otherwise; every $y\in R$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,y=\ell$ and $y\otimes 1$ lying in $\mathcal{S}_\ell$ admits a unique $x\in S$ with $y=ux$ for some two-sided unit $u$ of $R$ of reduced norm $1$; and the multiset of matrices underlying $H_\ell$ is the image of $S$ under $\iota$. Moreover, for each prime $\ell$, each $\gamma$ in `fuchsianGroup R ι` (the image under $\iota$ of the group generated by the units of $R$, intersected with the determinant-one subgroup) and each $\tau$ in the upper half-plane, the multisets $\{\Gamma\cdot(\delta\gamma\tau):\delta\in H_\ell\}$ and $\{\Gamma\cdot(\delta\tau):\delta\in H_\ell\}$ of $\Gamma$-orbits coincide, where $\Gamma=$ `fuchsianGroup R ι`.
--
--   This packages the classical Hecke correspondence data for an Eichler order in an indefinite rational quaternion algebra: a finite system of representatives, modulo left multiplication by norm-one units, of the elements of reduced norm $\ell$ whose diagonal idele is Hecke-admissible, together with the fact that the resulting many-valued map on the upper half-plane is well defined on the quotient by the Fuchsian group. It supplies the Hecke family and descent hypotheses used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_fuchsianGroup`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_fuchsianGroup).
